 these  magical beasts which is why he chooses  to ride one wherever he goes bone uppers  tend to live in Dragon graveyards and  for the longest time they were thought  to be extinct so could the Boneknapper  be the armored wings long-lost relative  we think so and here's why armored wings  and bone appers are both  Street class dragons who prefer to live  in solitude they have soft scales that  need protection causing them to search  for Armour wherever they go  whereas a Boneknapper goes for bones and  armor wink seeks out metal they have  similar horns and lethal tails and  they're both known for having pale green  skin  however some armored wings are orange  and funny enough sightings of orange  bone Nappers have been documented  however seeing one is super rare so do  we have you convinced if so it looks  like Aaron and snotlout's dragons might  be distant cousins of some sort the Game  of Thrones theory a year after the first  How to Train Your Dragon movie came out  and HBO TV series called Game of Thrones  took the world by storm and while both  these productions had many similarities  one stuck out above all dragons when we  were first introduced to hiccup he's a  timid and clumsy guy who wants nothing  more than to make his father proud but  instead of slaying dragons and becoming  the Viking everyone wants him to be he  befriends dragons and learns how to ride  them a popular fan theory is that hiccup  horrendous is none other than Daenerys  Targaryen 'he's ancient relative in fact  some might say that hiccup is  responsible for the entire Valyrian race  Vikings it's an occupational hazard How  to Train Your Dragon takes place in a  pre medieval setting which fits right  into the game of Thrones timeline on top  of that hiccups a natural when it comes  to handling dragons which could be a  gene that was passed down from  generation to generation  more than that hiccup is bound to marry  Astrid and have kids of his own one day  so perhaps Astrid super fair hair was  carried down in the gene pool creating  the classic valerian look we've all come  to know if you've got your valerian  history down pack then surely you  remember how Valyria was placed in a  desolate part of the world far away from  modern civilization and you'd also know  that malaria was wiped off the face of  the earth when the doom came for the  small islands so could it be that the  Isle of Berk eventually became valaria  and that hiccup and asteroids relatives  escaped to dragons edge for refuge if so  this means that dragons edge and drag  stone are one in the same but with  slightly different names  if hiccups descendants are in fact the  Targaryen then it makes sense that they  would have access to a land in Westeros  after all dragons edge is said to be a  thirty four hour trek from the Isle of  birth oh and here's a coincidence we  just can't ignore actor Kit Harington  who plays Jon Snow in Game of Thrones  also please air it in How to Train Your  Dragon so if this isn't enough to get  you guys on board with this theory we  don't know what is Malka the Scythian  warrior at the beginning of the first  How to Train Your Dragon movie we  learned that hiccups mother was killed  by a dragon when he was just a baby okay  well we learned that she was taken by a  dragon but by Viking law being taken by  a dragon and being killed by one  basically meant the same thing however  during How to Train Your Dragon 2 we  find out that Belka is very much alive  and thriving in a dragon utopia although  Valka is allegedly a Viking there are  some fan theories surrounding her  heritage or rather her fake parentage a  reddit member that goes by the name of  observa wrote a theory that put Falcons  background on the stand and most of her  evidence is too spot-on to be wrong  according to observe Alka isn't a Viking  but rather a Scythian female warrior and  here's why for starters Viking women  weren't allowed to be warriors in fact  they hardly ever joined their husbands  in battle at all instead they stayed  home to raise children and take care of  trivial matters but when it comes to  Scythian warriors women were known for  their excellent fighting skills and  since palca is often referred to as an  amazing warrior we're inclined to think  that she's not a Viking at all Scythian  people live during the same time as the  Vikings did and were known for being  nomadic people who were fond of writing  huge horses in battle Vikings on the  other hand had no love for horses and  preferred to do their bidding on boats  so could it be that stoic and Valka met  and fell in love against all odds we  have to save the Dragons if so it could  explain my balcony like an outcast while  living on the Isle of birth after all  why would she want to run away from her  hometown newborn son and husband  if she was born and raised a Viking from  where we're standing it looks like she  longed for her old life back  but what's forbidden to continue being  the fierce warrior she was raised to be  so when a dragon came to carry her off  she saw it as a way to start a new and  better life an alpha named toothless  although dogs and Dragons are  significantly different they do have  some things in common  mainly they both do whatever their alpha  commands them to do in How to Train Your  Dragon 2 we found out the hard way that  toothless was no match for the bewilder  beasts commands and sadly he blasted  stoic with his fiery powers causing him  to pass away shortly after though  toothless snapped out of his trance and  challenged the alpha to save hiccup from  an untimely death so how did a tiny  dragon take on a big old blue wildebeest  well a popular fan theory is that  toothless was an alpha in the making all  along you just didn't know it yet do you  guys remember when toothless took on the  Red Death in the first how to train your  dragon movie well if you do then surely  you recall how the Red Death was the  Alpha of her path and as the hierarchy  goes dragons who successfully be alphas  take their place at the top knowing this  it makes total sense that other dragons  chose to coexist with the Vikings after  the big battle after all why would any  of them want to live with the Vikings  after being hunted by them for  generations the popular theory is that  toothless is the alpha dragon a bird  however whether or not he was aware of  this is a question we don't have answers  to but once he made the choice to snap  out of the blue wildebeest trance he  began to glow a deep blue before  challenging the Alpha and eventually  beating him so the moral of the story is  that toothless has been an alpha since  the first movie but this assumption  leaves room for suspicion which leads us  into our next Theory toothless the  double agent here's a theory that you  might not fall in love with but hey lame  the internet not us the popular fan  theory is that toothless is a double  agent of some sorts in the first film  hiccup uses his brilliant mind to  fashion a dragon killing device however  after firing it he realizes that killing  dragons  feel as good as he thought it would with  a guilty conscience  hiccup locates toothless and nurses him  back to health and to make up for his  bad deed he creates a device that allows  toothless to fly but there's a catch the  harness is only effective if he controls  it while he's on his back having little  to no options toothless welcomes the  friendship despite knowing that it's  hiccup who shot him down so later on  when it comes time for toothless to save  hiccup from the fiery pits he purposely  latches on to his leg which results in  him losing it so despite saving hiccup  he gets even with him an eye for an eye  right well not quite because the score  is not even yet and here's how the Alpha  Theory ties into the double agent one  despite loving hiccup toothless despised  stoic and how could he not after all he  did murder hundreds of dragons during  his lifespan however killing stoic  out-of-the-blue was too risky so  toothless pretended to be under the  bewilder beasts mind-control knowing  full well that stoic would sacrifice  himself for hiccup this way he could get  his revenge without being punished for  it although we believed toothless to be  as harmless as a puppy we can't deny  that stoic Steph was a little suspicious  after all  toothless came out of his trance for  hiccup a few scenes later but would have  obliterated him seconds before the Isle  of fireproof Vikings believe it or not  that there are some fans who believe  that hiccup and its people are indeed  fireproof or fire resistant at best  while it's true that hundreds of Vikings  have been killed by dragons there's  hardly ever record of them being burnt  to a crisp instead people were eaten  alive or carried away by them on more  than one account we see hiccup and his  friends come inches away from huge  flames without showing any signs of  discomfort if these Vikings could  actually feel the burn they'd be jumping  off their dragons backs as soon as a  flame was thrown their way to support  that notion let's think back to stoic  stead although toothless's blast did  result in him passing away he wasn't  phased in the slightest proving that his  skin wasn't affected by the fire however  toothless says  whoo plasma blast was more than  effective on top of that we all saw  hiccup fall into a field of fire but  this accident only resulted in the loss  of his lower leg and nothing else in  fact every single hair on his head was  intact despite falling headfirst into  the flames this theory sheds even more  light on the targaryen theory at the  beginning of this video which toys with  the notion that the targaryen are  descendants of the Haddock's  this makes complete sense considering  that the targaryen are immune to fire as  well so there you have it guys the six  craziest theories surrounding the How to  Train Your Dragon franchise before you  go let us know which theories you agree  with and which ones do you think are  hogwash and that's a wrap make sure to  subscribe to the things to be first in  line to watch our newest videos thanks  for watching and see you next time  [Music]

